    "created_at": "2022-12-30T14:57:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-12-30T14:59:58Z",
    "body": "The issue is caused by the new `sso_session` key, which is not discoverable by `starship` yet.\r\n\r\nBtw:\r\n```\r\n[default]\r\n...\r\n\r\n[profile default]\r\n...\r\n```\r\ndoesn't make sense anyway, you should have only one profile named `default` - the first one.\r\n\r\n> You can specify one default profile that is used when no profile is explicitly referenced. Other profiles have names that you can specify as a parameter on the command line for individual commands. Alternatively, you can specify a profile in the [AWS_PROFILE](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/userguide/cli-configure-envvars.html) environment variable which overrides the default profile for commands that run in that session.\r\n\r\nhttps://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/userguide/cli-configure-profiles.html",
    "author_association": "NONE",
